   "points": 21,
   "problemType": "observation",
   "statement": "The equatorial constellations are listed below. Fill in the missing ones in the correct order. Use the IAU codes or official names accepted by the IAU.\n\n| Number | Constellation |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 | Serpens (Ser) |\n| 2 | Ophiuchus (Oph) |\n| 3 | __________ |\n| 4 | Aquarius (Aqr) |\n| 5 | Pisces (Psc). |\n| 6 | Cetus (Cet) |\n| 7 | __________ |\n| 8 | __________ |\n| 9 | __________ |\n| 10 | Monoceros (Mon) |\n| 11 | Canis Minor (CMi) |\n| 12 | __________ |\n| 13 | __________ |\n| 14 | __________ |\n| 15 | Virgo (Vir) |\n\nWhich of these 15 constellations are also on the ecliptic? If you give more than the required number of constellations, only the first ones you write (in order) will be considered.",
   "parts": [],
   "solution": {
    "statement": "**Filling missing Equatorial constellations:**\n\n| Number | Answer | Points |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | Aql (Aquila) | 2 |\n| 7 | Tau (Taurus) | 2 |\n| 8 | Eri (Eridanus) | 2 |\n| 9 | Ori (Orion) | 2 |\n| 12 | Hya (Hydra) | 2 |\n| 13 | Sex (Sextans) | 2 |\n| 14 | Leo (Leo) | 2 |\n\n**Ecliptic constellations are following:**\n\n| Answer | Points |\n| --- | --- |\n| Aqr (Aquarius) | 1 |\n| Leo (Leo) | 1 |\n| Oph (Ophiuchus) | 2 |\n| Psc (Pisces) | 1 |\n| Vir (Virgo) | 1 |\n| Tau (Taurus) | 1 |",
